HomeRow -- third-party material
===============================

HomeRow is GPL-3.0-or-later; everything bundled with it must be compatible
with that.

Content
-------

HomeRow/Resources/Lessons/gtypist/*.typ
    The lessons of GNU Typist, https://www.gnu.org/software/gtypist/,
    unmodified.  Copyright (C) 1998-2003 Simon Baldwin, (C) 2003-2022 the
    GNU Typist contributors; GPL-3.0-or-later.  kt*.typ derive from KTouch
    and ttde.typ from TippTrainer; each file names its source and authors.
    See the README in that folder for the exact commit.

HomeRow/Resources/Languages/*/words-*.txt
    Word lists from MonkeyType, https://github.com/monkeytypegame/monkeytype,
    Copyright (C) the MonkeyType contributors; GPL-3.0.  Imported by
    Scripts/import-monkeytype.py; the LICENSE file in each pack names the
    source files and the commit.  The exception is english/words-200.txt,
    which was compiled by hand for HomeRow.

HomeRow/Resources/Sounds/*/*.wav
    HomeRow's own: synthesized sample by sample by Scripts/make-sounds.py,
    nothing recorded or borrowed.  GPL-3.0-or-later, like the program.

HomeRow/Resources/Layouts/*.plist
    Keyboard layouts from MonkeyType (same project, licence and commit),
    converted by Scripts/import-monkeytype-layouts.py; see Layouts/LICENSE.

HomeRow/Resources/Code/Files/<language>/*
    Source files for code mode, copied unmodified from the projects below
    by Scripts/import-code.py.  Each keeps its own copyright notice; the
    licence texts are in HomeRow/Resources/Code/LICENSES, and index.plist
    records repository, path, commit and licence per file.  All of these
    licences are compatible with GPL-3.0-or-later.

    valkey-io/valkey             BSD-3-Clause
    lua/lua                      MIT
    AFNetworking/AFNetworking    MIT
    Mantle/Mantle                MIT
    SDWebImage/SDWebImage        MIT
    dotnet/runtime               MIT
    JamesNK/Newtonsoft.Json      MIT
    python/cpython               PSF-2.0
    psf/requests                 Apache-2.0
    expressjs/express            MIT
    jashkenas/underscore         MIT
    microsoft/vscode-textmate    MIT
    golang/go                    BSD-3-Clause
    spf13/cobra                  Apache-2.0
    rust-lang/rust               MIT OR Apache-2.0
    BurntSushi/ripgrep           MIT OR Unlicense
    jOOQ/sakila                  BSD-2-Clause
    rbenv/rbenv                  MIT
    ohmyzsh/ohmyzsh              MIT
    nvm-sh/nvm                   MIT

HomeRow/Resources/Code/Grammars/*.tmLanguage.json
    TextMate grammars, unmodified, from the extensions bundled with
    Visual Studio Code (https://github.com/microsoft/vscode, MIT), which
    takes each from an upstream project of its own; all MIT.  Grammars/NOTICE
    names every upstream and commit.

    Not used: MonkeyType's quotes, which are excerpts from third-party
    works, and Typing.io's content, which is proprietary.

Compiled in
-----------

HomeRow/ThirdParty/oniguruma
    Oniguruma, https://github.com/kkos/oniguruma, the regular expression
    library TextMate grammars are written for.  Copyright (c) 2002-2021
    K.Kosako; BSD 2-clause, see COPYING in that folder.  Unmodified apart
    from a hand-written config.h; README.HomeRow there names the commit.

HomeRowTests/Fixtures/textmate (tests only, not shipped in the app)
    The tokenizer test cases of vscode-textmate,
    https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-textmate, Copyright (c) Microsoft
    Corporation; MIT.  They in turn come from Atom's first-mate (MIT).

Linked at run time
------------------

FreeCoreData (GNUstep builds only)
    https://github.com/ashalkhakov/FreeCoreData
    MIT licence; a port of the Cocotron CoreData runtime (Copyright (c)
    2006-2009 Christopher J. W. Lloyd, Johannes Fortmann and the other
    Cocotron contributors named in FreeCoreData's LICENSE files), with
    NSFetchedResultsController following MRTFetchedResultsController by
    Matteo Rattotti (MIT).
    The commit used is pinned in .github/scripts/dependencies.sh.

GNUstep (libobjc2, libs-base, libs-gui, libs-back), libdispatch, the Eau
theme and the DejaVu and Liberation fonts are shipped inside the AppImage
under their own licences; none of their source is part of this repository.

